{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And He will stretch out His hand against the north</b> — And He mentioned Assyria; this is a sign that it is north of the land of Israel. And if Nineveh was Atruyeih [Nineveh], its breadth from the equator is forty-two degrees, and the breadth of Jerusalem is thirty-three degrees, which is half of the inhabited world toward the north, with complete proofs."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The place name אטרויי\"ה appears to be a transliteration of a geographical name, possibly 'Atroyeh' or similar; rendered as in the Hebrew with a bracketed identification of Nineveh for context, though the exact source form is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:22.112802227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}